  "b6_reason": "For a wire in equilibrium under a single weight W at its free end, tension is uniform along its length and equals W at every cross-section, so stress = W/A.",
  "b6_working": "Consider any cross-section at distance x from the support. The part of the wire below it (of negligible weight) is in equilibrium under tension T (upward) and W (downward), so T = W. Stress = T/A = W/A.",
